Done — `sum.go:3`. Three changes, all behavior-preserving:

- **`range` instead of an index loop** — removes the `i < len(xs)` bounds bookkeeping and the `xs[i]` indexing, so there's no off-by-one to check.
- **`t` → `total`** — the name says what it accumulates.
- **`t = t + xs[i]` → `total += x`** — the idiomatic compound form.

Added a doc comment noting the empty-slice case, since `Sum` is exported.

